--------------------------------------------------------------------------

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE EXAMPLES (.env.example)

This file serves as a template for your actual .env file, which should

never be committed to version control. Set these values in your local .env

for development, and use secure secrets management for production.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

==================================

1. CORE APPLICATION CONFIGURATION

==================================

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000

Secret key used for session management and token signing

JWT_SECRET=a_very_long_and_random_string_of_characters_for_security

==================================

2. DATABASE CONFIGURATION

==================================

Replace with your actual database connection string

DATABASE_URL="mongodb://localhost:27017/public_safety_db"

or for SQL: "postgres://user:password@host:port/dbname"

==================================

3. IOT DEVICE & TELEMETRY

==================================

IoT Platform Connection Details (e.g., Google Cloud IoT Core, AWS IoT, Azure IoT Hub)

IOT_BROKER_HOST=https://www.google.com/search?q=mqtt.exampleiotplatform.com
IOT_DEVICE_ID_PREFIX=PSTZ_SENSOR_
IOT_API_KEY_SECRET=your_iot_platform_api_key

==================================

4. AI/ML MODEL ENDPOINTS

==================================

Endpoint for the Alert Verification Model (e.g., to confirm a real emergency)

AI_VERIFICATION_ENDPOINT=https://www.google.com/search?q=https://ai.model-service.com/api/verify
AI_MODEL_AUTH_TOKEN=secure_token_for_ai_api

==================================

5. GEOSPATIAL & DISPATCH SERVICE

==================================

API key for mapping service (e.g., Google Maps, Mapbox) for proximity dispatch

MAP_API_KEY=your_geospatial_service_key
DISPATCH_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:4000/dispatch
DISPATCH_SERVICE_SECRET=internal_dispatch_auth_secret
